  "sport": "bandy",
  "title": "Full speed round the centre circle and shoot",
  "description": "The players stand in two queues by the boards on each side, just inside their own half of the centre line. A cone stands along each board a way up towards the goal. The coach places a stationary ball a little outside the penalty area and has more balls ready. Goalkeeper in goal.\n\nA skates at full speed up to the cone, rounds it, skates back down and round the centre circle, comes up to the ball and shoots straight at goal. When A shoots, B starts from the other side and skates the same course mirrored. The coach puts out a new ball after each shot. Switch queues after each turn.\n\nDo not start too close together – the goalkeeper must have time to set before each shot. The diagram is not to scale.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "High tempo all the way – it is a skating drill with a finish."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "Lean in and hold your speed round the cone and round the circle."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "Look at the ball when you shoot, you know where the goal is."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp4",
      "text": "Fetch your ball if the shot goes wide."
    }
  ],
